     },
     "literals": [
      "70"
     ],
     "text": "**Chapter 70 is general aid.** The state pays it into the town’s general fund toward the school budget, and it may be spent on anything that budget covers. Lunenburg was held at the formula’s minimum-aid floor in FY2022, FY2024, FY2025, FY2026."
    },
    {
     "figures": {},
     "literals": [],
     "text": "**Every grant is categorical.** It may be spent only on the purpose it was given for, and most are paid after the money is spent. So the two are shown side by side here, never added into one total."
    },
    {
     "figures": {},
     "literals": [],
     "text": "**Allocated is not spent.** An allocation is what DESE says the district may draw; spending is what the ledger shows. Different stages, never subtracted."
    }
   ],
   "place": "chart",
   "title": "General aid and grants",
   "tone": "define"
  },
